@page "/mcp-server"

@* Describes the MCP server this demo's host maps at /mcp. Its route differs from the endpoint's on
   purpose: two literal endpoints on /mcp would make a GET of it ambiguous. *@

<PageTitle>MCP server</PageTitle>

<h1>MCP server</h1>

<p class="page-intro">
    This site hosts a Model Context Protocol server at <code>/mcp</code>, so an AI agent building tours
    with Bit.Bonboarding reads the library itself - its compiled API documentation, its guide, its
    stylesheet and these demo pages - instead of guessing at an API it half remembers. Every tool is
    read-only.
</p>

<section class="demo-section">
    <h2>Connect a client</h2>

    <p>
        The endpoint is plain Streamable HTTP, so any MCP client connects with a URL and nothing else. The
        same tools are also served, version by version, through the bit platform's own server at
        <code>https://bitplatform.dev/mcp</code>, next to the other bit libraries.
    </p>

    <pre><code>@ClientConfig</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="demo-section">
    <h2>Tools</h2>

    <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it answers</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>SearchBonboarding</code></td>
                    <td>Everything at once - the guide, every public member, the theme variables and the demo sources - each hit with the exact follow-up call.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>GetBonboardingSetupGuide</code></td>
                    <td>The complete wiring for one render mode: server, wasm, auto or standalone-wasm.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>GetBonboardingGuideSection</code></td>
                    <td>One section of the reference guide, or the index of sections.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>GetBonboardingApi</code></td>
                    <td>One public type with every parameter, property and method, its real default and its documentation - or the index of types.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>GetBonboardingThemeVariables</code></td>
                    <td>Every <code>--bit-bonboarding-*</code> variable with its light and dark value.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>InspectBonboardingPlacement</code></td>
                    <td>Where the library's own placement engine puts a popover for a given target, popover and viewport, and why.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>GetBonboardingSourceFile</code></td>
                    <td>One demo file verbatim - every page here is a working tour - or the index of files.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <p>
        The guide, the API, the theme and the sources are also exposed as <code>bonboarding://</code> resources,
        and three prompts - <code>add-bonboarding-to-app</code>, <code>implement-bonboarding-tour</code> and
        <code>debug-bonboarding-tour</code> - walk an agent through the common jobs in the right order.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="demo-section">
